From 9261bcd51365fa6b31be86eb371b73358786e84f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeong, Heon" <blmarket@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:45:00 -0700
Subject: Fix memory leak when losing client

path field should be freed when losing a client. server_client_lost
frees every other string the client owns, including title, which
set-titles sets beside path in server_client_set_path; path itself is
freed only where it is replaced, so the last one a client held goes with
it.

The pane decides how long that string is: it arrives as OSC 7 from
whatever is running in the pane, and input-buffer-size lets that be a
megabyte.

Applies to 3.7b unchanged; server_client_lost frees title and cwd in the
same place there.
---
 server-client.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/server-client.c b/server-client.c
index 52886f01..640b7eb4 100644
--- a/server-client.c
+++ b/server-client.c
@@ -475,6 +475,7 @@ server_client_lost(struct client *c)
 	input_cancel_requests(c);

 	free(c->title);
+	free(c->path);
 	free((void *)c->cwd);

 	evtimer_del(&c->repeat_timer);
